From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:11:40 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Port aurora-silicon/m1n1's merged change #40 (3eade8e3)

nvme: quiesce ANS AP power in stage 1 on T8132 only

aurora-silicon/m1n1 #40 (aurora-silicon/ryan/j713-stage1-ans-36),
merged as 3eade8e3, ported as its merge diff against the first parent.
It carries one commit:

  2bfc58d7 nvme: quiesce ANS AP power in stage 1 on T8132 only

It limits #36's stage-1 AP quiesce to chip_id == T8132. It applies
without conflicts on top of the #36 port.

Build (RELEASE=1 CHAINLOADING=1, clang/lld 23.1.4): no new warnings.
test_nvme_adoption.py and test_m4_ans_fdt.py pass.

Hardware tested on: NOT YET
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 src/nvme.c | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nvme.c b/src/nvme.c
index f1941347..8c8373e4 100644
--- a/src/nvme.c
+++ b/src/nvme.c
@@ -731,11 +731,14 @@ bool nvme_shutdown(void)
 #if defined(CHAINLOADING) && !defined(ESP_STAGE2)
         /* Stage 2 and U-Boot adopt this session without servicing its mailbox
          * (only Linux takes RTKit ownership again), so stop the IOP pushing
-         * log traffic at the AP before handing it on. */
-        if (nvme_rtkit && rtkit_quiesce_ap(nvme_rtkit))
-            printf("nvme: ANS AP power quiesced for the next stage\n");
-        else
-            printf("nvme: could not quiesce ANS AP power; later stages may stall\n");
+         * log traffic at the AP before handing it on. Only T8132 has run
+         * this; the other M4-generation chips keep their stage 1 hand-off. */
+        if (chip_id == T8132) {
+            if (nvme_rtkit && rtkit_quiesce_ap(nvme_rtkit))
+                printf("nvme: ANS AP power quiesced for the next stage\n");
+            else
+                printf("nvme: could not quiesce ANS AP power; later stages may stall\n");
+        }
 #endif
         nvme_adopt_live_session = true;
         nvme_initialized = false;
